<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zahir al-Din Mar'ashi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zahir al-Din Mar'ashi was a Persian historian of the 15th century from the Mar'ashi family of sayyids who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a>. He wrote histories of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruyan">Ruyan</a> and Mazandaran and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a>, which are the main sources for the local dynasties of the Caspian provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p></div>
